class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: the published line count opens the file its first argument names, reads it through core/io's line reader, counting a last line without its newline and a line too long for the buffer, prints the count through a buffered writer, and would say a failure in words through failure.words on standard error
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
run_files: input.txt
run_expect: output.txt
stream: output
status: 0
constructs: 0790, 0800, 0940, 0960, 1030, 1100, 1650, 1660
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64
